---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Logo from '../components/Logo.astro';
---
<Layout title="Support policy — TabMonger" description="How optional one-time support for TabMonger works.">
  <main class="legal shell">
    <a href="/" class="brand-link"><Logo /></a>
    <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Support policy</p>
    <h1>Optional means optional.</h1>
    <p class="legal-lede">TabMonger is free and open source, built by an independent developer dad. A contribution is a voluntary, one-time show of support; it does not purchase software, unlock features, create a subscription, or promise future work.</p>
    <section>
      <h2>Payments</h2>
      <p>Checkout and payment processing are hosted by Stripe. TabMonger’s website never receives or stores card or bank information. The amount is chosen by the supporter within the limits shown at checkout.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Not tax-deductible</h2>
      <p>TabMonger is not a charitable organization. One-time contributions are optional project support and are not tax-deductible.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Refunds</h2>
      <p>If a payment was made by mistake, use the contact details on the Stripe receipt to request help. Never post card information or a full payment receipt in a public issue.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Questions about the software</h2>
      <p>For bugs and feature requests, use the project’s <a href="https://github.com/truedezigner/tabmonger/issues">GitHub issue tracker</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <a class="button" href="/">← Return home</a>
  </main>
</Layout>
